CP/M 2.2 Copyright and License
=================================

This distribution contains a modified CP/M 2.2 CCP/BDOS core
originally developed by Digital Research, Inc. The core is based on
the reconstruction by Clark A. Calkins (February 27, 1981), adapted
from the PC-9801 CP/M-80 project. See cpm22/cpm22_fm11.asm.

CP/M and its derivatives are made available under the permission
granted by Bryan Sparks, President of DRDOS, Inc., as clarified on
July 9, 2022.

The current CP/M license information is available at:

    http://www.cpm.z80.de/license.html

The 2022 permission grants a nonexclusive right to use, distribute,
modify, enhance, and otherwise make available CP/M and its
derivatives.

CP/M is not placed in the public domain by this distribution.
Copyright and other rights in the original CP/M materials remain
with their respective rights holder(s).

The FM-11-specific bootstrap, CBIOS, utilities, and other
original files in this distribution are separate works and are
licensed under the terms stated elsewhere in this package.

